Do not set up the shadow call stack (x18) on arm64 in the ANDRUNA build.

On Windows ARM64, x18 is the platform register and always points to the
thread environment block; writing it breaks every Windows call made by
the thread. Bionic allocates a shadow call stack for each thread and
stores its address in x18 (spike S4). Android's app code does not use
shadow call stacks, and nothing in the guest is built with
-fsanitize=shadow-call-stack, so under ANDRUNA on arm64 the set-up is
skipped and x18 is left alone.

diff --git a/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp b/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp
--- a/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp
+++ b/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@
 }
 
 static void __init_shadow_call_stack(pthread_internal_t* thread __unused) {
-#if defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__riscv)
+#if (defined(__aarch64__) && !defined(ANDRUNA)) || defined(__riscv)
   // Allocate the shadow call stack and its guard region.
   char* scs_guard_region = reinterpret_cast<char*>(
       mmap(nullptr, SCS_GUARD_REGION_SIZE, PROT_NONE, MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON, -1, 0));
